{"t":184,"text":" Read the story"}
{"t":204,"text":"\n\nPriya had always wanted a"}
{"t":225,"text":" garden, but the flat she"}
{"t":247,"text":" shared with her grandmother"}
{"t":266,"text":" had only one small window ledge"}
{"t":286,"text":". Every morning she carried"}
{"t":306,"text":" a chipped blue jar"}
{"t":328,"text":" to school in her backpack,"}
{"t":348,"text":" and every afternoon she chec"}
{"t":369,"text":"ked it again.\n\nInside"}
{"t":395,"text":" the jar was a single sun"}
{"t":409,"text":"flower seed. Her gr"}
{"t":430,"text":"andmother had given it to her"}
{"t":450,"text":" on the day they moved in."}
{"t":470,"text":" \"Seeds are patient"}
{"t":491,"text":",\" Grandma said. \""}
{"t":511,"text":"They wait until they are ready"}
{"t":532,"text":" to grow.\"\n\nPriya"}
{"t":554,"text":" did not feel patient. She"}
{"t":574,"text":" watered the jar every day,"}
{"t":593,"text":" even"}
{"t":614,"text":" though the soil looked dry"}
{"t":637,"text":". She read books about plants and"}
{"t":661,"text":" drew pictures of a t"}
{"t":678,"text":"all yellow flower."}
{"t":696,"text":" Her classmate Tomas"}
{"t":719,"text":" laughed at her. \""}
{"t":738,"text":"Nothing is happening,\" he"}
{"t":757,"text":" said.\n\nOne Saturday"}
{"t":779,"text":", a thunderstorm"}
{"t":798,"text":" rattled the windows. When"}
{"t":819,"text":" Priya woke up, she"}
{"t":841,"text":" noticed a small green sho"}
{"t":860,"text":"ot poking through the soil."}
{"t":881,"text":" It was no taller than her little"}
{"t":901,"text":" finger. She ran to the"}
{"t":921,"text":" kitchen, where Gr"}
{"t":942,"text":"andma was making tea."}
{"t":963,"text":"\n\n\"It's growing!\""}
{"t":984,"text":" Priya shouted."}
{"t":1005,"text":"\n\nGrandma smiled and set"}
{"t":1026,"text":" down her cup. \"Now"}
{"t":1046,"text":" you must give it light and water,"}
{"t":1065,"text":" and then wait a little longer"}
{"t":1085,"text":".\"\n\nOver the next wee"}
{"t":1108,"text":"ks, the shoot grew"}
{"t":1126,"text":" into a sturdy stem"}
{"t":1147,"text":" with two broad leaves."}
{"t":1168,"text":" Priya moved the jar"}
{"t":1188,"text":" to the window every morning so the"}
{"t":1209,"text":" plant could catch the sun"}
{"t":1229,"text":". Tomas came to see"}
{"t":1249,"text":" it one afternoon and was"}
{"t":1270,"text":" surprised at how tall it"}
{"t":1290,"text":" had become.\n\n\"Mayb"}
{"t":1312,"text":"e I should start a garden too"}
{"t":1331,"text":",\" he said quietly."}
{"t":1353,"text":"\n\nPriya grinned. \""}
{"t":1373,"text":"Seeds are patient,\""}
{"t":1393,"text":" she reminded him.\n\n="}
